/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 736 Tm (Accumulation describes how repeated attention and practice build a pattern over time. A) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 721 Tm (single reflection may feel modest, yet a series of observations can reveal what supports) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 706 Tm (your direction. The principle points toward patient consistency, not instant results or a) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 691 Tm (promise of a particular outcome.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 668 Tm (7. Constructiveness) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 634 Tm (Constructiveness asks whether your thinking leads toward useful action. It is not forced) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 619 Tm (optimism. It means identifying what can be built, repaired, clarified or practised next,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 604 Tm (even when a situation is imperfect. Constructive attention turns reflection into a choice) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 589 Tm (that can be tested in real life.) Tj
